# CRC Pull Secret
#
# This file should contain your Red Hat pull secret for CodeReady Containers (CRC).
#
# To obtain your pull secret:
# 1. Go to https://console.redhat.com/openshift/create/local
# 2. Log in with your Red Hat account
# 3. Click "Download pull secret"
# 4. Copy the entire JSON content into a file named 'pull-secret.txt' in this directory
#
# The pull secret should look like this (this is just an example structure):
# {
#   "auths": {
#     "cloud.openshift.com": {
#       "auth": "...",
#       "email": "..."
#     },
#     "quay.io": {
#       "auth": "...",
#       "email": "..."
#     },
#     "registry.connect.redhat.com": {
#       "auth": "...",
#       "email": "..."
#     },
#     "registry.redhat.io": {
#       "auth": "...",
#       "email": "..."
#     }
#   }
# }
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Never commit your actual pull-secret.txt file to version control
# - The pull-secret.txt file is already in .gitignore
# - Keep your pull secret secure as it contains authentication credentials

